# Milestone: M3
# Covers: nested '&' and '|' separator combinations; complex join-tree evaluation.
# blocked: `&` is a statement separator, not an expression operator.
#          Probed: `var r = 42 & 51` is a parse error, so the join-tree
#          VALUE this fixture asserts cannot be captured or echoed.  The
#          nested-fork EXECUTION works (see separator/block_operands.chk);
#          what is missing is the value of a join.
#
# Everything below this line predates the re-foundation: it names
# tasks and entry points that no longer exist, and its account of
# what stands in the way has been superseded by the `blocked:` line
# above, which was probed against this branch.  Kept for the
# original urbiscript it carries.
# matrix-row: separator-and
#
# Reason:
#   '&' (OP_FORK_JOIN) requires the realm-managed scheduler path.  The chk
#   runner uses the urbi_vm_run REPL path (realm == NULL); OP_FORK_JOIN produces
#   a TypeError in that context.  This fixture exercises deeply nested '&'/'|'
#   interleaving which depends on correct multi-strand scheduling.
#
# Original urbiscript (activate at M5 with urbi_step chk driver):
# # {1|5}&{2|6|9|10}&{3|7}&{4|8};
# # 42&51;
